{"id": "section-body-29305", "title": "Axial Spondyloarthritis", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-six", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "RHEUMATOLOGICAL DISORDERS", "Inflammatory Arthritis", "Axial Spondyloarthritis"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-29305", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Axial Spondyloarthritis", "runs": [{"text": "Axial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Spondyloarthritis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "105"}}, {"id": "body-29306", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A chronic inflammatory rheumatic disease that primarily affects the sacroiliac joints and spine, leading to pain, stiffness, and progressive fusion of the axial skeleton, resulting in reduced spinal mobility.", "runs": [{"text": "A chronic inflammatory rheumatic disease that primarily affects the sacroiliac joints and spine, leading to pain, stiffness, and progressive fusion of the axial skeleton, resulting in reduced spinal mobility."}]}, {"id": "body-29307", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It is usually classified as:", "runs": [{"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "classified"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as:"}]}, {"id": "body-29309", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Non-radiographic axSpA (nr-axSpA): No structural damage seen on X-ray. MRI may show active inflammation of the sacroiliac joints (SIJ)", "runs": [{"text": "Non-radiographic axSpA (nr-axSpA): No structural damage seen on X-ray. MRI may show active inflammation of the sacroiliac "}, {"text": "joints (SIJ)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "97"}}, {"id": "body-29310", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Radiographic axSpA / Ankylosing Spondylitis (AS): Structural damage to SIJ visible on X-ray (per modified New York criteria). Progressive spinal fusion may occur.", "runs": [{"text": "Radiographic"}, {"text": "